# WandB console logs are deliberately never versioned.
#
# r11's alone is 368,020,804 B, above GitHub's hard 100 MB per-file limit, and a
# console log contributes nothing to the per-step curves that this directory
# exists to serve -- every plotted series lives in history.csv.  Git would also
# keep the blob forever, taxing every future clone, with no way to drop it short
# of rewriting history.  WandB retains these server-side, so re-pull on demand
# with the wandb-export skill instead.
#
# This rule exists so that a stray `git add -A` cannot commit one by accident.
console.log
*/console.log
